        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dmitri Usatov, Antonín Dvořák, Adolf Čech, Marie Červinková-Riegrová\n- Works: Eugene Onegin, The Devil and Kate\n- Roles: Lensky\n- Topics: opera production, composer collaborators\n\nFacts:\n- Dmitri Usatov sang the role of Lensky in an opera.\n- The role of Lensky is in Eugene Onegin.\n- The composer of The Devil and Kate was Antonín Dvořák.\n- The Devil and Kate had contributions from Antonín Dvořák’s friends Adolf Čech and Marie Červinková-Riegrová.\n- The Devil and Kate therefore had more contributions from friends of its composer than Eugene Onegin, as stated in the comparison.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
